                <pb facs="0802" n="788" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg788"/>

                <head><seg type="margin">[62]</seg> *<hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish, Secretary of State, to Mr. Boutwell, Secretary of the Treasury.</hi></head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1869-05-25"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 25,
                        1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Mr. Thornton, the British minister
                    accredited to this Government, having represented to me that the steamer Quaker
                    City is laden with flour, that she has been transferred to a British subject and
                    is bound for Jamaica, I submit to you the propriety of instructing the collector
                    of customs at New York to interpose no obstacles to her departure, upon bonds
                    being given that she will not engage in any proceedings which will give aid or
                    support to any parties prosecuting hostile movements against any government with
                    which that of the United States is at peace.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, yours, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">George S. Boutwell</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of the Treasury.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
